      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Restorative justice has a more morally sound foundation in modern social justice movements. It focuses on repairing harm, promoting healing, and holding individuals accountable for their actions, rather than solely punishing offenders for retribution. This approach acknowledges the harm caused to vulnerable groups, particularly victims, and prioritizes their needs and involvement in the healing process. Restorative justice seeks to build bridges and promote collective understanding, whereas retributive justice often perpetuates cycles of punishment and cycles of harm. This shift in perspective aligns with contemporary efforts to address systemic injustices and promote social justice.",
